{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Vapor.</b> It is possible that the word הבל is two forms: one with the pattern of זהב, and the second the known one, with the pattern of ארץ, like ויעל עשנו כעשן הכבשן, and ויסמך בצרי כמו חלב עזים. Some say that הבל is an imperative, and the matter is like עזוב, and the definite ה comes upon Qohelet because it is an adjective of the noun, for it does not come upon a proper noun. And when he mentioned the death of man, he said: it is now clear to you what I said to you at the beginning — הבל הבלים."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {0 "Resolved ה״א as הה״א (the letter heh); עצ׳ as עצם (substance/proper noun), reading לא יבא על שם העצם as 'it does not come upon a proper noun.'"}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:29:20.807896248Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}